 <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Is applying for a business credit card with no revenue hard?</h3><p>No. Applying for a business credit card with no revenue works like any card application: you enter $0 revenue, the issuer checks your personal credit and income, and you sign a personal guarantee.</p><h3>Can you get a business credit card with no revenue?</h3><p>Yes. Most issuers approve based on your personal credit and income, so you can enter $0 business revenue and still qualify by signing a personal guarantee. <a href="https://www.chase.com/personal/credit-cards/education/basics/business-credit-card-no-revenue" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Major issuers confirm this</a>.</p><h3>What credit score do you need for a business credit card with no revenue?</h3><p>A personal FICO score of about 670 or higher is the practical bar for most personal-guarantee business cards. Secured business cards accept lower or limited scores.</p><h3>Can an LLC with no income get a credit card?</h3><p>Yes &mdash; a brand-new LLC with no income can apply. Approval rests on the owner&#39;s personal credit and income, not the LLC&#39;s sales, and you&#39;ll typically sign a personal guarantee.</p><h3>Do you have to enter revenue on a business credit card application?</h3><p>You enter your business revenue, but $0 (or a realistic projection) is acceptable for a startup. Issuers weigh your personal income and credit far more heavily at this stage.</p><h3>Can you get a business card with no personal guarantee?</h3><p>Rarely for brand-new companies. No-personal-guarantee cards (startup/corporate cards) usually require meaningful cash in a linked <a href="https://learners-link.blogspot.com/2026/07/how-to-open-business-bank-account.html">business bank account</a> or investor funding.</p><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@graph": [{"@type": "BlogPosting", "headline": "Best Business Credit Cards With No Revenue (2026 Guide)", "about": "busines